Each standalone page is authoritative for that module's complete description,
instructions, compatibility notes, changelog, and individual download.


REQUIREMENTS
------------

- Starfield 1.16.244.0
- SFSE 0.2.20 or later
- Address Library for SFSE Plugins for Absolute Control
- OpenTrack only when Absolute Head Tracking is selected and used
- A DirectInput joystick, throttle, pedals, or button box only when needed by
  the selected gameplay modules


INSTALL / UPDATE
----------------

Install @ARCHIVE_NAME@ normally with a FOMOD-capable mod manager such as MO2 or
Vortex. Absolute Control is required by this installer; every gameplay module
is optional.

The archive includes only mod-owned runtime files. It does not include or
overwrite user-owned custom INIs, HOTAS Profiles, logs, PDBs, research builds,
or retired Absolute Workbench descriptors.

When updating, keep and back up:

- AbsoluteControlPanel_Custom.ini
- AbsoluteHOTAS_Custom.ini
- AbsoluteHOTAS Profiles directory
- AbsolutePower_Custom.ini
- any other user-created module configuration or profiles

Installing a standalone module over the all-in-one is supported when it is a
newer compatible version. Do not enable a second copy of the same DLL from a
different mod-manager entry.


MODULE SELECTION NOTES
----------------------

- AbsoluteHOTAS has no axis bindings by default. Configure it in Absolute
  Control before expecting flight input.
- Absolute Power ships optional preset shortcuts on number keys 1-4 during
  flight. Change or clear them if they conflict with another setup.
- Absolute Head Tracking requires OpenTrack with FreeTrack 2.0 Enhanced output.
- AbsoluteZero Mouse Steering is enabled by default and changes mouse-flight
  centering immediately. Select it deliberately.


QUICK START
-----------

1. Install the archive and choose the modules you want.
2. Launch Starfield through SFSE.
3. Open the Pause Menu and select MOD OPTIONS.
4. Open each installed module and review its bindings and enabled state.
5. Apply changes, close the menu, and test in a safe flight context.


COMPATIBILITY CONTRACT
----------------------

- Absolute Control owns presentation, menu navigation, capture dialogs, and
  shared host registries.
- Gameplay modules own their configuration, runtime behavior, validation,
  fallback policy, and failure behavior.
- Missing optional modules do not disable the remaining suite.
- Missing or incompatible Absolute Control does not make a gameplay module a
  mandatory load-time dependency; supported standalone fallbacks remain owned
  by each module.
- Version-specific native operations fail closed when their runtime gates do
  not validate.


KNOWN BETA BOUNDARIES
---------------------

- Hardware combinations, duplicate DirectInput device names, overlays, and
  third-party ship-control mods may expose behavior not present in the
  maintainer setup.
- Controller-only navigation and some compound record workflows need broader
  public hardware coverage.
- Power automation remains disabled by default and is not part of the supported
  beta feature promise.
- Head tracking is rotational only; translation is not implemented.


ROLLBACK
--------

Disable or uninstall the all-in-one, then reinstall the previous standalone
versions you were using. Restore user-owned custom files only if a test save
changed them in an unwanted way.


REPORTING FEEDBACK
------------------

Include the Absolute Suite manifest, Starfield and SFSE versions, selected
modules, hardware/tracker names, exact reproduction steps, and the relevant
module log with logging enabled. Sanitize custom configuration before sharing.

Source and issue tracker:
https://github.com/SultanDesync/Absolute-Control


